{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.MesonKaonPionHeckeSeifert","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.MesonKaonPionHeckeSeifert","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Units.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.mesonMassRatio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.mesonMassRatio","kind":"def","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/meson-kaon-pion-hecke-seifert.lean#L96-L99","doc":"The meson mass ratio formula:\nm_K/m_π = χ^{(2,1)}(σ₁⁵) × (9/5)². ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.seifert_ratio_T25_T23","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.seifert_ratio_T25_T23","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/meson-kaon-pion-hecke-seifert.lean#L83-L94","doc":"Seifert volume ratio V_S(T(2,5)) / V_S(T(2,3)) = 9/5, over any field\nin which 2, 3, 5 are invertible. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:meson-kaon-pion-hecke-seifert","label":"prop:meson-kaon-pion-hecke-seifert","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/meson-kaon-pion-hecke-seifert.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.seifertEuler","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.seifertEuler","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/meson-kaon-pion-hecke-seifert.lean#L79-L81","doc":"Seifert Euler number of T(2,n): e = 1 - 1/2 - 1/n = (n-2)/(2n). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.quarkConstituentCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.quarkConstituentCount","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/meson-kaon-pion-hecke-seifert.lean#L57-L73","doc":"The number of quark constituents of a meson, which is the squaring\nexponent appearing in `mesonMassRatio`.  A **named constant**, not a\ntheorem.\n\nReplaced `theorem meson_squaring_exponent : (2 : ℕ) = 2 := rfl`\n(2026-08-21; vacuity ledger, `reflexive-tautology-ascribed-literal`).\nThe docstring named an equality of two defined quantities — the\nsquaring exponent and the constituent count — but the Lean proved\n`2 = 2`, dropping both sides; it held whatever either quantity was.\nPer Strict Lean Discipline §8 that is notation, not a theorem.\n\nThe identification is now carried **structurally** instead of being\nasserted: `mesonMassRatio` raises `(9/5)` to this constant, so the\nexponent *is* the constituent count by construction rather than by a\ntautology claiming so. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.chi_21_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.chi_21_odd","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/meson-kaon-pion-hecke-seifert.lean#L47-L53","doc":"For odd n, χ^{(2,1)}(σ₁ⁿ) = qⁿ - q⁻ⁿ. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.chi_21","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.chi_21","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/meson-kaon-pion-hecke-seifert.lean#L41-L45","doc":"Hecke character χ^{(2,1)}(σ₁ⁿ) = qⁿ + (-q⁻¹)ⁿ for the standard\nrepresentation of H₃(q), with `q` carried as a unit so `q⁻¹` is the\n`Units` inverse rather than a field division. For odd n, this equals\nqⁿ - q⁻ⁿ. ","signatureChunk":0}]}